# Who makes YummyOrange's releases, pinned so a release can't go out signed by another team or with another update key.
# Installed copies would refuse such a release, and only a manual reinstall would fix them. build.sh and
# Tools/updates/release.sh read this file (KEY=value lines; nothing in it is run) and refuse anything else.
# Public values only: no secret ever goes in here.
#
# TEAM_ID            The team of the Developer ID Application certificate that signs releases. 37P86CG9SS is the team
#                    of this Mac's Apple Development certificate; a Developer ID certificate of the same Apple account
#                    carries the same team. release.sh refuses a SIGN_IDENTITY whose name ends in another "(TEAM)".
# UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY  The update key's public half, base64, as make-update-keys.swift prints it. Before the first
#                    release, add the public half of a backup key kept off this Mac, after a space, so the key can be
#                    replaced later without stranding installed copies (they trust every key listed here). Empty until
#                    the key is made: release.sh refuses to run without it.
# FEED_URL           The update feed's real address, ending in /updates/appcast.json: on yummyorange.com, the domain
#                    YummyOrange owns (a custom domain you own is safest: a vercel.app name that is given up can be
#                    taken by someone else, and every copy built with it keeps asking it). build.sh builds it into every
#                    copy, and release.sh refuses any other address.
TEAM_ID=37P86CG9SS
UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY=
FEED_URL=https://yummyorange.com/updates/appcast.json
